ss":"claude-code_2-1-308_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Coordination note 2026-11-09 (PST): ADR number 0123 is yours. Gerrit change 3337 (fix-versions release field, epic inferior-seaborgium-aruanas) briefly claimed 0123 too; it is now renumbered to 0124, so no change on your side is needed. Please don't take 0124.","timestamp":1794264797255247001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed as Gerrit change 3338 (WIP, hashtag rebar-session-a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d), patch set 1 = 93a8eea08703cd96b35c233df5f7e82ab4159aaf. make verify exited 0 at 15:45 PST (20,847 + 202 passed). gen_adr_index.py --check and check_adr_numbers.py both exit 0. Status is Proposed: it flips to Accepted once the operator confirms the three open decisions it marks (engine switch key/default/precedence; agentic runtime and read-only enforcement; budget and timeout). Held in WIP for the 0.14.1 release; not to be submitted until RELEASED.","timestamp":1794267944518912001}],"created_at":1794255546198920001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"709ca956-c5d0-4e75-99c6-a8446b13eb91","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c584-b8b9-999f-4358"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe parent epic adds a second plan-review engine (a single-agent Opus 5.5 review) beside the current 4-pass pipeline (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py`, `passes.py`, `pass1.py`), and upgrades the configured models to the 5.5 generation. Several of its choices are one-way doors that later children build on: the config key that selects the engine, how the agent is run and kept read-only, how its findings become today's verdict and sidecar, and how a signed attestation records which engine produced it. Those choices need one durable record before the engine children are planned against them, and the epic's first acceptance criterion requires an ADR under `docs/adr/`.\n\n## Approach\n\nWrite one ADR, `docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md`, then run `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py`, which derives both the marker `docs/adr/.numbers/0123` and the index `docs/adr/README.md` from `docs/adr/*.md` (`scripts/gen_adr_index.py:5-16`; the README's line 3 says it is generated and must not be hand-edited). The docs gate runs `gen_adr_index.py --check` (`.github/actions/docs-gates/action.yml:32`) and `scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` asserts the marker bijection. It follows the repo's ADR shape (`docs/adr/0122-similar-ticket-retrieval.md`: Status, Date, Context, Decision, Consequences). An ADR fits because every decision below is hard to reverse once attestations carry it and later children code against it; a ticket comment would not be found by the next reader of `docs/adr/`.\n\nStatus is **Proposed** while the three operator decisions marked (D) below are open; each (D) section states the recommended default the ADR adopts unless the operator chooses otherwise, and flipping to **Accepted** is the last edit before landing. The ADR records, one section each:\n\n1. **Engine switch** (D): key `[verify] plan_review_engine` (beside the existing plan-review keys `require_plan_review_for_claim` and `require_plan_review_for_close` in `rebar.toml` `[verify]`), values `\"pipeline\"` (today's 4-pass engine) and `\"agentic\"`, default `\"pipeline\"` so no project changes behaviour without opting in. Precedence: an explicit per-call `engine` argument on the library entry point (used by the CLI `--engine` flag, the MCP start tool and the comparison harness) over the `rebar.toml` key over the built-in default. No environment variable. The key carries a `mechanism-ok: config_key` marker naming the open sunset ticket under the epic, because the switch exists only until one engine is retired.\n2. **Agentic engine design** (D): one call on rebar's existing runner in `execution_mode=\"agentic\"` (`src/rebar/llm/runner.py:58`, `RunRequest`), frontier model class, so the Bedrock-first provider chain and fallback apply unchanged and no CI provider or subscription is needed (`project.portability`). Tools are exactly the runner's existing read-only surface: `pai_tools.filesystem_tools` (`read_file`, `list_directory`, `search_files`), `grounding_tools`, and `rebar_tools` with comment withheld (`runner.py:380-390`). Read-only is enforced three ways: the surface contains no write or execute tool, `fs_tools._safe_path` refuses traversal (`src/rebar/llm/fs_tools.py:24`), and the read root is the gate-chosen snapshot `assert_gated` requires (`runner.py:362-369`). Budget and timeout (D): `tool_step_limit=60` (steer to a final answer), `iteration_limit=80`, model-maximum output tokens and per-request timeout `cfg.timeout_s` — existing `RunRequest` fields (`runner.py:95-102`) and config (`config.py:355`), no new knob. Effort is not an engine setting: the agent inherits the per-model effort table the sibling upgrade ticket `beaten-natural-grouse` introduces (Opus 5.5 at `high`).\n3. **Severity-to-verdict mapping** (decided 2026-11-09 on the epic): the adapter sets each finding's `decision`, the key `orchestrator.finalize_verdict`'s partition reads (`orchestrator.py:296-299`): `blocker` becomes `decision: \"block\"`; `major`, `minor` and `trivial` become `decision: \"advisory\"`. Severity alone decides; the criterion's registry posture does not, so a blocker labelled with an advisory-posture criterion still blocks. Zero blockers is PASS; a run that fails or returns unparseable output is INDETERMINATE through the same `resolution_class` path as a failed pipeline pass. The agentic engine has no Pass-2 verify or Pass-3 decide step, so no priority or decision margin is computed; those fields are absent, as they are for DET findings.\n4. **Finding schema mapping**: the prompt's finding object (`id`, `title`, `description`, `severity`, `evidence`, `suggested_fix`) gains a `criteria` list of registry criterion ids (possibly empty), matching the `criteria` list the pipeline's findings carry (`sidecar.py:621`). The adapter maps `title` + `description` to `finding`, `evidence` to `evidence`, `suggested_fix` to `suggested_fix`, keeps `severity`, drops ids not in `registry.by_id()`, and sets `decision` per section 3; ids are minted with `orchestrator.mint_finding_id`. With `decision` set, `finalize_verdict` and the sidecar readers consume the findings unchanged.\n5. **Engine provenance on the attestation**: the signed plan-review attestation (`plan_review/attest.py`) gains an `engine` field inside the signed payload; an attestation without it reads as `\"pipeline\"`, so every existing attestation stays valid for claim, close, `review-plan --status` and `sign-review`.\n6. **Invariants both engines keep**: the Layer-1 floor (`floors.py`, `det_*.py`) and claimability (`claimability.py`) run first and unchanged; if either stops the review, no LLM call is made and the result is identical under both engines.\n7. **Model upgrade**: Opus 4.8, Sonnet 4.6 and Haiku 4.5 move to Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5 and Haiku 5.5, with sampling parameters withdrawn and `effort` set explicitly (`high` for Opus and Sonnet, `medium` for Haiku); the call-by-call audit lives on the sibling upgrade ticket `beaten-natural-grouse` and the ADR links it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md (new)\n- docs/adr/.numbers/0123 (generated by `scripts/gen_adr_index.py`)\n- docs/adr/README.md (regenerated by `scripts/gen_adr_index.py`)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md` exists with one section for each of the seven numbered decisions above, each (D) section stating its adopted default, and Status Accepted at landing.\n- [ ] `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` exits 0.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md","reason":"new ADR"},{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers/0123","reason":"ADR number marker"},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"index row"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"],["relates_to","c584-b8b9-999f-4358"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"b48f2cd6-7fba-450f-9d45-e1338bd42191","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"11f7-cf57-be02-4441","ticket_type":"task","title":"ADR 0123: selectable plan-review engine, agentic design, verdict mapping, engine provenance, 5.5 model upgrade","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1d56d0aa-f7f2-4364-b0e7-3c48dd30a646","35bdaa7b-317f-4076-b75b-3d3a19d7402c","1679807f-25d7-4654-af64-9ff34aa46454","5df0ee16-eddc-411b-9796-ac6e74241b36","b48f2cd6-7fba-450f-9d45-e1338bd42191","21c1439e-68c6-47c6-9671-62dafbd20835","01c0e769-140a-456b-95d8-e5a5dddd7f97","8b7524c9-cf27-4b15-a0f4-fab9d9d65fdf","709ca956-c5d0-4e75-99c6-a8446b13eb91"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794268150252346612,"uuid":"f34d6077-a4db-41eb-887d-faccec04f1f1"}